	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg6433"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=15" title="View the profile of Killy">Killy</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Goddess of Whips and Rezzes<br />
								Moderator<br />
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 448<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://home.comcast.net/~nlfalkowski/ss/clericanim02.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/KillyCirce" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="KillyCirce" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=Lepredes"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=Lepredes&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="Lepredes" border="0" /></a>
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=15"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.echoesineternity.org/" title="EIE" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6433#msg6433"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6433#msg6433">Re:You've got to be kidding me...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #21 on:</b> March 24, 2004, 08:28:15 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I have a 10 year old daughter, her name is Carlyn. &nbsp;She has a learning disability and so for her in her 5 &nbsp;years of school has never seen a honor roll. &nbsp;And yes they do the honor roll at her age. &nbsp;She sits and talks to me and wishes she could be better at something than some of the other kids. &nbsp;She is a beautiful child and from looking at her you could never tell. &nbsp;But she cannot run as fast, she cannot spell as fast and she cannot answer questions as fast as some of the other kids. &nbsp;Yes some of the kids look down on her, but she is popular not because she can&#039;t do things as fast as other but because she is the sweetest child you could meet. &nbsp;I do believe that if they are gonna have the honor roll or other things they should still look at children that even if they are modified they should still get a chance. &nbsp; So we finally bought our first brand new home this past week and we move there before the beginning of the next school year. &nbsp;I hope at the new school that she will go to she will get a better chance at being on the honor roll so she can say she won something. &nbsp;That is what she wants and I will stand by her and if she does not get on the honor roll or makes the fastest runner or something I will give her a award. &nbsp;I think the biggest thing is that children who grow up in big families dont get noticed alot at home so that is why they look to wanting to being on honor roll ... &nbsp;Some it is not that way.......... oh well, thought i would just post something on here about this because I know I am in the position with my own child..... /hugs Killy
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><div align="center"><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=1100304" target="_blank"><img src="http://kilaer.tripod.com/sitebuildercontent/sitebuilderpictures/kilaer-1.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><span style="color: Teal;">What we do in life, &quot;Echoes in Eternity&quot;</span></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg6436"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52" title="View the profile of Gabus">Gabus</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 276<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/psychotic-day.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I beat the Internet. The end guy was hard.<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6436#msg6436"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6436#msg6436">Re:You've got to be kidding me...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #22 on:</b> March 24, 2004, 08:37:39 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							At the risk of sounding like a jerk, I disagree Killy. Not because your child is not important, but because the nature of the honor roll is to recognize those academic achievers. The honor roll says nothing about the personality of those students on it. Many of the students on ours, I wouldn&#039;t take my eyes off of for 2 seconds in a classroom. Similarly, many have NO personality to speak of, as many spend all of their day studying, and are severly lacking in social skills. Since the honor roll is not focused on the WHOLE child, only one part, it is a skewed way to evaluate children.<br /><br />Rest assured that your student is actually getting a better education in socialization and how to get along with people. A skill that is sorely lacking in American society today. (and the primary reason i am against home-schooling) Your daughter should win awards and recognition for her personality and sweetness, since that is what SHE excells at, not on the honor roll, which is about grades. You should push (along with other parents) for recognition of things OTHER than grades. It can be done. We have alternative methods of recognizing students at our school, and they work well too.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=139779" target="_blank">Gabus Magelo Profile</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
