	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg6559"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=187" title="View the profile of Diamsorn">Diamsorn</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Leader<br />
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 36<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=187"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.blessedrebellion.org" title="Blessed Rebellion" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6559#msg6559"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6559#msg6559">Re:You've got to be kidding me...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #24 on:</b> March 31, 2004, 01:25:46 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I have a dissabled child as well, who doesn&#039;t run as fast as others, doesn&#039;t spell as fast as others infact we are extactic that he spells some days. &nbsp;<br /><br />He&#039;s 13. &nbsp;<br /><br />He comes to me on a daily basis and wishes he could bring home a blue ribbon, or trophy so that I would be proud of him. &nbsp;<br /><br />Damn I&#039;m proud of him in the fact that every day he&#039;s up at 5:45 am to get ready for school that starts at 8:15 am and is with in walking distance. &nbsp;<br /><br />I try to tell him everyday how proud I am of him that he brought home a 63 in english, his 1st ever grade in english cause his teachers finally decided it was important to teach him sentance structure, and other grammer rules.<br /><br />Will he ever be on the honor role? &nbsp;No<br />Will he ever win a spelling be? No<br /><br />I&#039;m happy that parents who&#039;s children excel in the academic area&#039;s of life recieve recognition through thier children. &nbsp;I&#039;m happy that parents who&#039;s children excel in sports recieve recognition through thier children.<br /><br />I&#039;m extatic that just the other day I saw my 13yr old son help a lady with her grocieries cross the street after she dropped a bag. &nbsp;He had to put down his bike to do this.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Diamsorn Se&#039;Clure<br />65 Forrest Stalker<br />Blessed Rebellion
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg6575"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402" title="View the profile of Callon">Callon</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 320<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Warpig<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6575#msg6575"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6575#msg6575">Re:You've got to be kidding me...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #25 on:</b> April 01, 2004, 11:49:22 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							The bottom line is that the need to recognize the achievements of kids with disabilities does not preclude recognizing other achievements like the honor roll, excellence in sports, superb art skills, etc. &nbsp;As others have said here, some schools are actually quite good at recognizing the achievements of students with a variety of disabilities. &nbsp;It can be done. <br /><br />Take this quote from the original article in question -- <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">As a result, all Nashville schools have stopped posting honor rolls, and some are also considering a ban on hanging good work in the hallways -- all at the advice of school lawyers. </div><br />Have the schools also stopped displaying athletic trophies, recognizing high performers in sports, showing off good artwork, etc.? &nbsp;Why is academic work put on a different standard, especially given that at many schools it&#039;s one of the least recognized areas of excellence among the students themselves? &nbsp;You sure as hell don&#039;t get popular by being good at your school work. &nbsp;<br /><br />Many kids aren&#039;t good at sports or other recognized achievements, but they do excel in their studies. &nbsp;Why should that recognition be taken away from them? &nbsp; To say that because some are disadvantaged, none should be recognized is to do a great disservice to many of the kids.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg6579"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=187" title="View the profile of Diamsorn">Diamsorn</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Leader<br />
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 36<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=187"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.blessedrebellion.org" title="Blessed Rebellion" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6579#msg6579"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6579#msg6579">Re:You've got to be kidding me...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #26 on:</b> April 01, 2004, 01:19:45 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Kids need to be encouraged, recognized, motivated, and any other word you want to think of that fits along this theme.<br /><br />The world is tough enough alone with out us as parents helping bring our children, or others for that matter down.<br /><br />I&#039;m all for Honor Roles. &nbsp;Will my son ever be on the honor role? no. &nbsp;But I&#039;m extremly proud of him no matter what his grades are.<br /><br />Last night on my way in the door a neighbor came up to me and complimented me on how respectful my 13yr old son is, as he was with 3 other kids his age, and my son was the only one that was respectful to the adults there.<br /><br />That makes me proud.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Diamsorn Se&#039;Clure<br />65 Forrest Stalker<br />Blessed Rebellion
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg6580"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
